cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or workflow, please cite it using the metadata below."

title: "HML-LiDAR Cave Mapping"
type: software

authors:
  - family-names: Bassetto
    given-names: Samuel
    affiliation: "Polytechnique Montréal, LABAC"
  - family-names: Beltrame
    given-names: Giovanni
    affiliation: "Polytechnique Montréal"

abstract: >-
  HML-LiDAR is an open-source helmet-mounted LiDAR/IMU workflow for cave
  mapping. RevA combines ROS 2 field acquisition using a Livox Mid-360 and
  Raspberry Pi, DLIO LiDAR-inertial post-processing, optional retrospective
  ZUPT-assisted reinitialization, operator-guided multi-session registration
  with Pegar, revisable network assembly, point-cloud inspection and
  annotation, and VisualTopo-compatible topographic export.

keywords:
  - cave mapping
  - speleology
  - LiDAR
  - LiDAR-inertial odometry
  - ROS 2
  - DLIO
  - point cloud
  - multi-session registration
  - Pegar
  - VisualTopo
  - open-source hardware
  - reproducible workflow

